## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a practical, policy-driven KCA flow for multi-tenant systems, focusing on enrollment, policy enforcement, and edge caching without getting lost in high-level theory.

## Key Concepts

- Policy-driven certificate issuance per tenant
- Central CA integration and edge gateway rotation
- Revocation propagation and OCSP/CRL caching
- Auditing fields and failure modes

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-enrollment flow sketch
async function enrollTenantPolicy(tenantId) {
  const policy = await fetchPolicy(tenantId);
  const cert = await kca.issueCert({ tenantId, policy });
  storeCertLocally(tenantId, cert);
  return cert;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test policy updates with zero downtime?
- How would you simulate revocation propagation to edge gateways in offline environments?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests KCA at the edge with ephemeral function lifetimes, cross-region trust, and performance constraints. Probes attestation, certificate lifetimes, crypto agility, policy propagation, revocation, and observable handoff latency.

## Key Concepts
- Hardware-backed root of trust and remote attestation
- Short-lived per-function certificates with SPIFFE IDs
- Cross-region trust anchors and PQC crypto agility
- Per-tenant policy binding and revocation/auditing
- Geo-failover handoff and cold-start latency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: CSR to central KCA and renewal flow
function enrollFunctionCert(functionId) {
  const csr = createCSR({id: functionId, scope: 'edge'});
  const attestation = attestToRegionalBootstrap();
  const cert = centralKCA.requestCert(csr, attestation, ttl=300);
  installCert(cert);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure cold-start latency budgets in a geo-distributed setup?
- What failover metrics and alerting would you implement for handoff failures?
